title: Avoid duplicate fetches on the experimental collator protocol
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Follow-up to #11967. Hardens the validator side of the experimental collator protocol
    against fetching the same collation more than once and against mis-attributing a fetched
    collation to the wrong peer.

    * **Dedup co-advertised collations.** When several peers advertise the same collation, only
      one fetch is issued. This is a best-effort optimisation for honest peers; no correctness
      property depends on it (a redundant fetch is the only cost when it does not collapse).

    * **Account a fetched collation only once verified.** A collation occupies a claim-queue
      slot — and is attributed to the delivering peer (for inclusion credit or invalid-collation
      slashing) — only after it is verified against the advertised candidate and its persisted
      validation data. Previously it was recorded optimistically and undone on failure, which let
      one peer's failing delivery release a *different* peer's valid delivery of the same
      candidate, depending on response ordering — mis-attributing a slot or letting a candidate
      escape its slash.

    * **Parked ("blocked") collations no longer count towards capacity.** A collation whose parent
      isn't seconded yet (so its PVD can't be reconstructed and the collator didn't inline the
      parent head data) is parked for retry but holds no slot, and parking is bounded to one at a
      time. Otherwise a peer could occupy capacity it never fills by withholding the parent head
      data. This is a legacy path; collators that inline the parent head data (required for
      elastic scaling) never block.

    * **Drop the 300ms initial fetch delay (`MAX_FETCH_DELAY`).** It rarely applied in practice and
      could penalise slower honest builds; the protection it approximated is delivered by parallel
      fetching ([#11023](https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/11023)).

    All collator-protocol behaviour changes are contained to the experimental validator side.

    Separately, `polkadot-node-network-protocol` gains `Protocol::request_timeout()`, exposing the
    per-protocol request timeout previously hardcoded inside `Protocol::into_config` (configured
    values unchanged).
crates:
- name: polkadot-collator-protocol
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-node-network-protocol
  bump: minor
